% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: the garments and clothing accessories of Chapters 61
% and 62.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the textile part of the model covers the garments and clothing accessories
% of Chapters 61 and 62
rule textiles_scope_garment:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the good is a garment.


% the textile part of the model covers the garments and clothing accessories
% of Chapters 61 and 62
rule textiles_scope_accessory:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the good is a clothing accessory.

rule top_upper_body with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "are garments designed to cover the upper part of the body":
a garment is a top
    if the garment is an upper body garment.

rule top_kind with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Sweaters, pullovers, sweatshirts, waistcoats (vests) and similar articles":
a garment is a top
    if the family of the garment is top.

rule garment_by_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "ARTICLES OF APPAREL AND CLOTHING ACCESSORIES, KNITTED OR CROCHETED":
a good is a garment
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of garments.

% a top described only by what it is (an upper body garment) is a garment
rule garment_top with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "are garments designed to cover the upper part of the body":
a good is a garment
    if the good is an upper body garment
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind.

% a suit or an ensemble the ruling does not name by kind (a named one is a
% garment by its family, set of garments)
rule garment_suit with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "means a set of garments composed of two or three pieces made up":
a good is a garment
    if the good is a suit
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family.

rule garment_ensemble with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "means a set of garments (other than suits and articles of heading 6107, 6108 or 6109)":
a good is a garment
    if the good is an ensemble
    and it is not the case that
        the family of the good is a family.

rule accessory_by_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "ARTICLES OF APPAREL AND CLOTHING ACCESSORIES, KNITTED OR CROCHETED":
a good is a clothing accessory
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of clothing accessories.

% what a garment covers, for suits and ensembles (note 3)
rule covers_upper_top with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "one garment designed to cover the upper part of the body":
a garment covers the upper body
    if the garment is a top.

rule covers_upper_jacket with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "one suit coat or jacket the outer shell of which, exclusive of sleeves, consists of four or more panels, designed to cover the upper part of the body":
a garment covers the upper body
    if the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [suit-type jacket, outerwear].

rule covers_lower with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "consisting of trousers, bib and brace overalls, breeches, shorts (other than swimwear), a skirt or a divided skirt":
a garment covers the lower body
    if the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [trousers, skirt].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The kinds of goods, and the families the headings name. A kind a ruling
% names that is not listed here falls in no family: the good is then not
% described by any heading (the model abstains) until the list says where it
% belongs.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

outerwear is a family of garments, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski-jackets), windbreakers and similar articles".
