bandana falls in the family scarf, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Shawls, scarves, mufflers, mantillas, veils and the like".
handkerchief falls in the family handkerchief, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Handkerchiefs".
tie falls in the family tie, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Ties, bow ties and cravats".
bow tie falls in the family tie, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Ties, bow ties and cravats".
cravat falls in the family tie, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Ties, bow ties and cravats".
brassiere falls in the family brassiere, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Brassieres, girdles, corsets".
girdle falls in the family girdle, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Girdles and panty-girdles".
panty-girdle falls in the family girdle, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Girdles and panty-girdles".
corset falls in the family corset, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Brassieres, girdles, corsets".
suspenders falls in the family braces, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "braces, suspenders, garters and similar articles".
garters falls in the family braces, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "braces, suspenders, garters and similar articles".
braces falls in the family braces, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "braces, suspenders, garters and similar articles".
headband falls in the family other accessory, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Other made up clothing accessories".
sweatband falls in the family other accessory, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Other made up clothing accessories".
arm sleeves falls in the family other accessory, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Other made up clothing accessories".
sash falls in the family other accessory, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Other made up clothing accessories".
neck gaiter falls in the family other accessory, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Other made up clothing accessories".
dickey falls in the family part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "knitted or crocheted parts of garments or of clothing accessories".
part falls in the family part, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "knitted or crocheted parts of garments or of clothing accessories".

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Suits and ensembles (Chapter 61 note 3, Chapter 62 note 3). Section XI note
% 14: other sets of garments are classified garment by garment — a scenario
% describes each garment of such a set as a good of its own.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the same in Chapter 62 note 3(a)
rule note_61_3a_suit with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "must be of the same fabric construction, color and composition; they must also be of the same style and of corresponding or compatible size":
a good is a suit of note 3
    if the components of the good are matching
    and a jacket is a component of the good
    and the jacket has at least four panels in its outer shell
    and the jacket covers the upper body
    and a lower garment is a component of the good
    and the lower garment covers the lower body
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the lower garment is bib overalls.

% the same in Chapter 62 note 3(b)
rule note_61_3b_ensemble with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "All of the components of an ensemble must be of the same fabric construction, style, color and composition; they also must be of corresponding or compatible size":
a good is an ensemble of note 3
    if the good is a set put up for retail sale
    and the components of the good are matching
    and an upper garment is a component of the good
    and the upper garment covers the upper body
    and a lower garment is a component of the good
    and the lower garment covers the lower body
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a suit.

rule suit_note_3 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "means a set of garments composed of two or three pieces made up":
a good is a suit
    if the good is a suit of note 3.

% A set the ruling itself calls a suit, of matching components, when it does
% not describe what note 3(a) reads (the jacket's panels): the ruling's
% characterisation, recorded as such ("the kind of S is suit").
rule suit_characterised with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "must be of the same fabric construction, color and composition; they must also be of the same style and of corresponding or compatible size":
a good is a suit
    if the kind of the good is suit
    and the components of the good are matching
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a suit of note 3.

% a set (a costume of a suit, a tie and a shirtfront) whose essential
% character the suit gives is classified as the suit (GRI 3(b))
rule suit_by_essential_character with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "shall be classified as if they consisted of the material or component which gives them their essential character":
a good is a suit
    if a component is a component of the good
    and the essential character of the good is given by the component
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
    and the component is a suit.

rule ensemble_note_3 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "means a set of garments (other than suits and articles of heading 6107, 6108 or 6109)":
a good is an ensemble
    if the good is an ensemble of note 3.

% the same for a set the ruling calls an ensemble
rule ensemble_characterised with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "All of the components of an ensemble must be of the same fabric construction, style, color and composition; they also must be of corresponding or compatible size":
a good is an ensemble
    if the kind of the good is ensemble
    and the components of the good are matching
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a suit
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an ensemble of note 3.

% the headings of suits and ensembles cover the set as such: the context
% requires it (Section XI note 14)
rule note_xi_14_suit with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "Unless the context otherwise requires, textile garments of different headings are to be classified in their own headings even if put up in sets for retail sale":
a good is classified as consisting of the good
    if the good is a set put up for retail sale
    and the good is a suit.

rule note_xi_14_ensemble with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "Unless the context otherwise requires, textile garments of different headings are to be classified in their own headings even if put up in sets for retail sale":
a good is classified as consisting of the good
    if the good is an ensemble.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6 and Section XI subheading note 2: a garment's subheading is decided by
% the textile material of what it is classified as (GRI 3(b)), and its fabric
% is that of the part that determines its classification.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule xi_construction with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "only the part which determines the classification under general interpretative rule 3 shall be taken into account":
the construction of a good is a construction
    if the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the fabric construction of the component is the construction.

% Which fabric a heading of Chapter 61 or 62 takes (note 1 of each chapter;
% heading 6212 whether or not knitted): for a good classified by GRI 3(c),
% the subheading reads the component whose fabric the chosen heading takes.
rule fabric_for_61 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "This chapter applies only to made up knitted or crocheted articles":
a good has a fabric for heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6101
    and the heading <= 6117
    and the fabric construction of the good is knitted.

rule fabric_for_62 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "excluding knitted or crocheted articles (other than those of heading 6212)":
a good has a fabric for heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6201
    and the heading <= 6217
    and it is not the case that
        the heading = 6212
    and it is not the case that
        the fabric construction of the good is knitted.

rule fabric_for_6212 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "whether or not knitted or crocheted":
a good has a fabric for heading 6212
    if the good is a good the model describes
    or the good is a component of an other good.

% a garment made up of a coated or nonwoven fabric (headings 6113 and 6210)
rule coated_fabric with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Garments, made up of fabrics of heading 5602, 5603, 5903, 5906 or 5907":
a garment is made up of coated fabric
    if the garment is made up of fabric of heading a heading
    and the heading is in [5602, 5603, 5903, 5906, 5907].

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Section XI note 2(A): a good of two or more textile materials is classified
% as if it consisted wholly of the one that predominates by weight over each
% other single textile material; when none predominates, as if it consisted of
% the one of the heading that occurs last in numerical order. Note 2(B)(b):
% first the chapter, then the heading within it — so the man-made fibres of
% Chapters 54 and 55 count together (2(B)(c)). Note 2(B)(a): a metalized yarn
% (heading 5605) is one textile material, whatever it is made of.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

cotton belongs to cotton, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 52, confer "CHAPTER 52 COTTON".
polyester belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
% elastane is a segmented polyurethane
elastane belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
% spandex is the American name of elastane, a segmented polyurethane
spandex belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
% nylon is a polyamide
nylon belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
polyamide belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
polypropylene belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
% acrylic fibres are polymers of acrylonitrile
acrylic belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers".
% modacrylic fibres are copolymers of acrylonitrile
modacrylic belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers".
rayon belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose) to produce polymers such as cuprammonium rayon (cupro) or viscose rayon".
viscose belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose) to produce polymers such as cuprammonium rayon (cupro) or viscose rayon".
cupro belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose) to produce polymers such as cuprammonium rayon (cupro) or viscose rayon".
% modal is a regenerated cellulose fibre
modal belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
% lyocell is a regenerated cellulose fibre
lyocell belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
% cellulose acetate is a chemically modified natural polymer
acetate belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By chemical modification of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose, casein and other proteins, or alginic acid), to produce polymers such as cellulose acetate or alginates".
triacetate belongs to man-made fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By chemical modification of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose, casein and other proteins, or alginic acid), to produce polymers such as cellulose acetate or alginates".
wool belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "means the natural fiber grown by sheep or lambs".
cashmere belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "Tibetan, Kashmir or similar goats".
alpaca belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
camel hair belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
mohair belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "Angora, Tibetan, Kashmir or similar goats".
angora belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
yak belongs to wool fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
silk belongs to silk, as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "CHAPTER 50 SILK".
flax belongs to vegetable fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "Flax, raw or processed but not spun".
% linen is flax
linen belongs to vegetable fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "Flax, raw or processed but not spun".
ramie belongs to vegetable fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "ramie".
hemp belongs to vegetable fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "True hemp".
jute belongs to vegetable fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "Jute and other textile bast fibers".
metalized yarn belongs to metalized yarn,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 56, confer "Metalized yarn, whether or not gimped, being textile yarn".

silk is a textile group of chapter 50,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "CHAPTER 50 SILK".
wool fibres is a textile group of chapter 51,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "CHAPTER 51 WOOL, FINE OR COARSE ANIMAL HAIR".
cotton is a textile group of chapter 52, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 52, confer "CHAPTER 52 COTTON".
vegetable fibres is a textile group of chapter 53,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 53, confer "CHAPTER 53 OTHER VEGETABLE TEXTILE FIBERS".
% counted as one chapter, numbered by the later of the two (55) when the last
% heading decides a tie
man-made fibres is a textile group of chapter 55,
    as stated in HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50, confer "When both chapters 54 and 55 are involved with any other chapter, chapters 54 and 55 are to be treated as a single chapter".
metalized yarn is a textile group of chapter 56,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 56, confer "CHAPTER 56 WADDING, FELT AND NONWOVENS; SPECIAL YARNS".

rule section_xi_2b_share with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "The choice of appropriate heading shall be effected by determining first the chapter and then the applicable heading within that chapter":
the share of a group in a garment is a total
    if the group is a textile group of chapter a number
    and the total is the sum of each percentage such that
        the garment contains the percentage percent of a material
        and the material belongs to the group.

rule section_xi_2ba_metalized with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "metalized yarn (heading 5605) are to be treated as a single textile material the weight of which is to be taken as the aggregate of the weights of its components":
the textile material of a garment is metalized yarn
    if all the yarn of the garment is metalized yarn.

rule section_xi_2a_predominance with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "are to be classified as if consisting wholly of that one textile material which predominates by weight over each other single textile material":
the textile material of a garment is a group
    if it is not the case that
        all the yarn of the garment is metalized yarn
    and the share of the group in the garment is a total
    and the total > 0
    and for all cases in which
            the share of an other group in the garment is an other total
            and it is not the case that
                the other group is equal to the group
        it is the case that
            the group at the total percent outweighs the other group at the other total percent.

rule section_xi_2a_weight with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "which predominates by weight over each other single textile material":
a group at a total percent outweighs an other group at an other total percent
    if the total > the other total.

rule section_xi_2a_tie with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "When no one textile material predominates by weight, the goods are to be classified as if consisting wholly of that one textile material which is covered by the heading which occurs last in numerical order":
a group at a total percent outweighs an other group at an other total percent
    if the total = the other total
    and the group is a textile group of chapter a number
    and the other group is a textile group of chapter an other number
    and the number > the other number.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Within the chapter, the heading (note 2(B)(b)): the subheadings of Chapters
% 61 and 62 name wool, fine animal hair and Kashmir goats (5101, 5102),
% synthetic and artificial fibres (5402/5503 before 5403/5504). A group with
% one class is its own class. Ties go to the later heading (the higher rank).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

synthetic fibres is a fibre class of man-made fibres ranked 1,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "staple fibers and filaments of organic polymers produced by manufacturing processes".
artificial fibres is a fibre class of man-made fibres ranked 2,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "used in relation to fibers, mean: synthetic: fibers as defined at (a); artificial: fibers as defined".
wool is a fibre class of wool fibres ranked 1,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "means the natural fiber grown by sheep or lambs".
cashmere is a fibre class of wool fibres ranked 2,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "Tibetan, Kashmir or similar goats".
fine animal hair is a fibre class of wool fibres ranked 3,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".

polyester is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
elastane is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
spandex is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
nylon is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
polyamide is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
polypropylene is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers to produce polymers such as polyamides, polyesters, polyolefins or polyurethanes".
acrylic is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers".
modacrylic is of the fibre class synthetic fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By polymerization of organic monomers".
rayon is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
viscose is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
cupro is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
modal is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
lyocell is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "By dissolution or chemical treatment of natural organic polymers (for example, cellulose)".
acetate is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "to produce polymers such as cellulose acetate or alginates".
triacetate is of the fibre class artificial fibres,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 54, confer "to produce polymers such as cellulose acetate or alginates".
wool is of the fibre class wool, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "means the natural fiber grown by sheep or lambs".
cashmere is of the fibre class cashmere, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "Tibetan, Kashmir or similar goats".
alpaca is of the fibre class fine animal hair, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
camel hair is of the fibre class fine animal hair, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
mohair is of the fibre class fine animal hair, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "Angora, Tibetan, Kashmir or similar goats".
angora is of the fibre class fine animal hair, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".
yak is of the fibre class fine animal hair, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 51, confer "the hair of alpaca, llama, vicuna, camel".

rule xi_2bb_class_share with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "then the applicable heading within that chapter, disregarding any materials not classified in that chapter":
the share of fibre class a class in a garment is a total
    if the class is a fibre class of a group ranked a rank
    and the total is the sum of each percentage such that
        the garment contains the percentage percent of a material
        and the material is of the fibre class the class.

% a group with a single class (cotton, silk, vegetable fibres, metalized yarn)
rule xi_2bb_single_class with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "The choice of appropriate heading shall be effected by determining first the chapter and then the applicable heading within that chapter":
the fibre material of a garment is a group
    if the textile material of the garment is the group
    and it is not the case that
        a class is a fibre class of the group ranked a rank.

rule xi_2bb_class with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "then the applicable heading within that chapter, disregarding any materials not classified in that chapter":
the fibre material of a garment is a class
    if the textile material of the garment is a group
    and the class is a fibre class of the group ranked a rank
    and the share of fibre class the class in the garment is a total
    and the total > 0
    and for all cases in which
            an other class is a fibre class of the group ranked an other rank
            and it is not the case that
                the other class is equal to the class
            and the share of fibre class the other class in the garment is an other total
        it is the case that
            the class at the total percent outweighs the other class at the other total percent.

% within a chapter, a tie goes to the class of the later heading
rule xi_2a_class_tie with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "which is covered by the heading which occurs last in numerical order among those which equally merit consideration":
a group at a total percent outweighs an other group at an other total percent
    if the total = the other total
    and the group is a fibre class of a parent ranked a number
    and the other group is a fibre class of the parent ranked an other number
    and the number > the other number.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Chapter 61 note 9, Chapter 62 note 9: left over right closure is men's,
% right over left women's, unless the cut clearly indicates the sex; a garment
% that cannot be identified goes to the women's headings.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Chapter 61 note 9 and Chapter 62 note 9: the closure rule does not apply
% when the cut shows the sex
rule note_61_9_cut with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "the cut of the garment clearly indicates that it is designed for one or other of the sexes":
the gender of a garment is a gender
    if the cut of the garment indicates the gender.

rule note_61_9_left_over_right with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Garments of this chapter designed for left over right closure at the front shall be regarded as men's or boys' garments":
the gender of a garment is men
    if it is not the case that
        the cut of the garment indicates a gender
    and the garment closes left over right.

rule note_61_9_right_over_left with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "those designed for right over left closure at the front as women's or girls' garments":
the gender of a garment is women
    if it is not the case that
        the cut of the garment indicates a gender
    and the garment closes right over left.

% a good that shows nothing of its sex itself — a set, a composite good — is
% of the sex of the component it is classified as consisting of (GRI 3(b))
rule note_61_9_component with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "shall be classified as if they consisted of the material or component which gives them their essential character":
the gender of a garment is a gender
    if a component is a component of the garment
    and the essential character of the garment is given by the component
    and it is not the case that
        the garment shows its gender
    and the component shows its gender
    and the gender of the component is the gender.

rule note_61_9_unidentified with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Garments which cannot be identified as either men's or boys' garments or as women's or girls' garments are to be classified in the headings covering women's or girls' garments":
the gender of a garment is women
    if it is not the case that
        the garment shows its gender
    and it is not the case that
        a component is a component of the garment
        and the essential character of the garment is given by the component
        and the component shows its gender.

rule shows_gender_cut:
a garment shows its gender
    if the cut of the garment indicates a gender.

rule shows_gender_left_over_right:
a garment shows its gender
    if the garment closes left over right
    and it is not the case that
        the cut of the garment indicates a gender.

rule shows_gender_right_over_left:
a garment shows its gender
    if the garment closes right over left
    and it is not the case that
        the cut of the garment indicates a gender
    and it is not the case that
        the garment closes left over right.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Chapter 61 note 4, Chapter 62 note 4: "Shirts" and "shirt-blouses" have long
% or short sleeves and a full or partial opening starting at the neckline;
% "blouses" are loose-fitting, may be sleeveless, with or without an opening.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule note_61_4_shirts with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "are garments designed to cover the upper part of the body, having long or short sleeves and a full or partial opening starting at the neckline":
a garment is a shirt
    if the garment is a top
    and it is not the case that
        the garment is sleeveless
    and the garment has an opening starting at the neckline.

rule note_61_4_blouses with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "are loose-fitting garments also designed to cover the upper part of the body but may be sleeveless and with or without an opening at the neckline":
a garment is a blouse
    if the garment is a top
    and the garment is loose-fitting.

% Note 4 defines shirts, shirt-blouses and blouses together; heading 6106 and
% 6206 cover all three
rule note_61_4_blouse_type with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "may also have a collar":
a garment is a blouse-type garment
    if the garment is a shirt
    otherwise the garment is a blouse.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Heading 6109. The Explanatory Note: T-shirts are lightweight knitted
% garments, not napped nor of terry, with long or short sleeves, without
% collar, without opening or fastening at the neckline, with a close-fitting or
% lower neckline; the heading also covers singlets and other vests. CBP adds,
% since HQ 950855 (1992), that the fabric be plain jersey or plain interlock.
% A tank top, for CBP, has the tank silhouette: straps, and a rear neckline
% below the nape of the neck (NY N360982).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the Explanatory Note to heading 6109 describes T-shirts as lightweight
% knitted garments, not napped nor of terry
rule en_6109_tshirt_fabric with provenance ruling NY N362034,
        confer "To be classifiable as a T-shirt, a garment must be constructed from lightweight, plain jersey or plain interlock fabric":
a garment has the fabric of a T-shirt
    if the fabric of the garment is lightweight
    and it is not the case that
        the garment is napped
    and it is not the case that
        the fabric of the garment is terry
    and the garment meets the knit test of its tariff for T-shirts.

rule cbp_hq_950855 with provenance ruling NY N362034,
        confer "plain jersey or plain interlock fabric; see Headquarters Ruling HQ 950855":
a garment meets the knit test of its tariff for T-shirts
    if the garment is classified under the US tariff
    and the garment is of plain knit fabric.

% EU offices apply the Explanatory Note to heading 6109 without CBP's plain
% jersey or interlock test
rule en_6109_eu_fabric:
a garment meets the knit test of its tariff for T-shirts
    if the garment is classified under the EU tariff.

% the Explanatory Note to heading 6109, as a French BTI quotes it: no opening
% or fastening at the neckline; the Note also excludes collars and has sleeves
rule en_6109_tshirt with provenance BTI FRBTIFR-BTI-2025-07379,
        confer "les vêtements repris à cette position ne doivent pas comporter de dentelles, d'ouverture à l'encolure ou de bouton ou autre système de fermeture":
a garment is a T-shirt
    if the garment is a top
    and it is not the case that
        the garment is sleeveless
    and the garment has the fabric of a T-shirt
    and it is not the case that
        the garment has a collar
    and it is not the case that
        the garment has a high neckline
    and it is not the case that
        the garment has an opening starting at the neckline.

rule cbp_tank_silhouette with provenance ruling NY N360982,
        confer "it lacks a tank silhouette. Specifically, as noted above, the rear neckline does not fall below the nape of the neck, and there is no appearance of straps in the back":
a garment has a tank silhouette
    if the garment has shoulder straps
    and the rear neckline of the garment falls below the nape of the neck.

rule cbp_tank_top with provenance ruling NY N360982,
        confer "Although you refer to the garment as a tank top, it lacks a tank silhouette":
a garment is a tank top
    if the garment is a top
    and the garment is sleeveless
    and the garment has a tank silhouette.

% the Explanatory Note to heading 6109 includes singlets and other vests:
% garments worn as undergarments
rule heading_6109_singlets with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "T-shirts, singlets, tank tops and similar garments, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is a singlet
    if the garment is a top
    and the garment is designed to be worn as an undergarment.

% a knitted undershirt is a singlet of heading 6109
rule heading_6109_undershirts with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "T-shirts, singlets, tank tops and similar garments, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is a singlet
    if the family of the garment is undershirt.

rule heading_6109_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "T-shirts, singlets, tank tops and similar garments, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is of the T-shirt family
    if the garment is a T-shirt
    otherwise the garment is a tank top
    otherwise the garment is a singlet.

% the exclusions of note 4 name these headings
heading 6105 is a shirt heading,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Headings 6105 and 6106 do not cover garments with pockets below the waist".
heading 6106 is a shirt heading,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Headings 6105 and 6106 do not cover garments with pockets below the waist".
heading 6205 is a shirt heading,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Headings 6205 and 6206 do not cover garments with pockets below the waist".
heading 6206 is a shirt heading,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Headings 6205 and 6206 do not cover garments with pockets below the waist".
heading 6105 is a knitted shirt heading,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "garments having an average of less than 10 stiches per linear centimeter in each direction".
heading 6106 is a knitted shirt heading,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "garments having an average of less than 10 stiches per linear centimeter in each direction".
heading 6105 excludes sleeveless garments,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Heading 6105 does not cover sleeveless garments".
heading 6205 excludes sleeveless garments,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Heading 6205 does not cover sleeveless garments".

% the same in Chapter 62 note 4 for headings 6205 and 6206
rule note_61_4_pockets with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Headings 6105 and 6106 do not cover garments with pockets below the waist":
a garment is excluded from heading a heading
    if heading the heading is a shirt heading
    and the garment has pockets below the waist.

% the same in Chapter 62 note 4 for headings 6205 and 6206
rule note_61_4_tightening with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "with a ribbed waistband or other means of tightening at the bottom of the garment":
a garment is excluded from heading a heading
    if heading the heading is a shirt heading
    and the garment has a means of tightening at the bottom.

rule note_61_4_stitches with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "garments having an average of less than 10 stiches per linear centimeter in each direction counted on an area measuring at least 10 cm by 10 cm":
a garment is excluded from heading a heading
    if heading the heading is a knitted shirt heading
    and the garment has less than ten stitches per centimetre in each direction.

% A top that does not reach the waist, or leaves the upper body largely
% uncovered (a crop top, a strapped top with limited coverage), is for CBP
% none of the tops of the shirt, blouse, T-shirt and sweater headings but an
% "other garment" (6114, 6211).
rule cbp_limited_coverage with provenance ruling NY N353571,
        confer "Based on the styling, length and coverage provided by this garment":
a garment is excluded from heading a heading
    if heading the heading is a heading of tops
    and the garment has limited upper body coverage.

heading 6105 is a heading of tops, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Men's or boys' shirts, knitted or crocheted".
heading 6106 is a heading of tops, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Women's or girls' blouses and shirts, knitted or crocheted".
heading 6109 is a heading of tops, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "T-shirts, singlets, tank tops and similar garments, knitted or crocheted".
heading 6110 is a heading of tops, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Sweaters, pullovers, sweatshirts, waistcoats (vests) and similar articles".
heading 6205 is a heading of tops, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Men's or boys' shirts".
heading 6206 is a heading of tops, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Women's or girls' blouses, shirts and shirt-blouses".

% the same in Chapter 62 note 4 for heading 6205
rule note_61_4_sleeveless with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Heading 6105 does not cover sleeveless garments":
a garment is excluded from heading a heading
    if heading the heading excludes sleeveless garments
    and the garment is sleeveless.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The group a subheading is chosen by: a suit, an ensemble, or the family of
% the good's kind; for hosiery, gloves, scarves the features the subheadings
% name. The chapters' tables read it with the heading, the gender and the
% fibre material.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% The subheadings of women's underwear name briefs and panties (6108.2x,
% 6208.9x); other underpants — boxers, boxer briefs, boyshorts, long
% underpants — are among the similar articles ("Other"). Men's underpants
% and briefs are named together (6107.1x, 6207.1x).
rule boxer_underpants with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Briefs and panties:":
a good is of boxer underpants
    if the family of the good is underpants
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind
        and the kind is in [briefs, panties].

rule group_boxer_underpants with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Briefs and panties:":
the subheading group of a good is boxer underpants
    if the good is of boxer underpants.

rule group_suit with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Suits:":
the subheading group of a good is suit
    if the good is a suit.

rule group_ensemble with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Ensembles:":
the subheading group of a good is ensemble
    if the good is an ensemble.

rule group_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "ARTICLES OF APPAREL AND CLOTHING ACCESSORIES, KNITTED OR CROCHETED":
the subheading group of a good is a family
    if it is not the case that
        the good is a suit
    and it is not the case that
        the good is an ensemble
    and the family of the good is the family
    and it is not the case that
        the family is in [panty hose, hosiery, gloves, scarf, handkerchief]
    and it is not the case that
        the good is of boxer underpants.

% a top described without a kind: its subheadings do not depend on the group
rule group_top with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Sweaters, pullovers, sweatshirts, waistcoats (vests) and similar articles":
the subheading group of a good is top
    if the good is an upper body garment
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is a kind.

% heading 6115 names graduated compression hosiery, panty hose and tights by
% the fineness of their yarn, and women's full-length or knee-length hosiery
rule group_compression with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Graduated compression hosiery (for example, stockings for varicose veins)":
the subheading group of a good is compression hosiery
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [panty hose, hosiery]
    and the good is graduated compression hosiery.

rule group_fine_panty_hose with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Of synthetic fibers, measuring per single yarn less than 67 decitex":
the subheading group of a good is fine panty hose
    if the family of the good is panty hose
    and it is not the case that
        the good is graduated compression hosiery
    and the yarn of the good measures a number decitex
    and the number < 67.

rule group_heavy_panty_hose with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Of synthetic fibers, measuring per single yarn 67 decitex or more":
the subheading group of a good is heavy panty hose
    if the family of the good is panty hose
    and it is not the case that
        the good is graduated compression hosiery
    and the yarn of the good measures a number decitex
    and the number >= 67.

rule group_panty_hose with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Other panty hose and tights:":
the subheading group of a good is panty hose
    if the family of the good is panty hose
    and it is not the case that
        the good is graduated compression hosiery
    and it is not the case that
        the yarn of the good measures a number decitex.

rule fine_hosiery with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Other women's full-length or knee-length hosiery, measuring per single yarn less than 67 decitex":
a good is fine womens hosiery
    if the family of the good is hosiery
    and it is not the case that
        the good is graduated compression hosiery
    and the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is in [stockings, knee-highs]
    and the gender of the good is women
    and the yarn of the good measures a number decitex
    and the number < 67.

rule group_fine_hosiery with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Other women's full-length or knee-length hosiery, measuring per single yarn less than 67 decitex":
the subheading group of a good is fine womens hosiery
    if the good is fine womens hosiery.

rule group_other_hosiery with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Panty hose, tights, stockings, socks and other hosiery":
the subheading group of a good is hosiery
    if the family of the good is hosiery
    and it is not the case that
        the good is graduated compression hosiery
    and it is not the case that
        the good is fine womens hosiery.

rule group_coated_gloves_plastics with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Impregnated, coated, covered or laminated with plastics or rubber":
the subheading group of a good is coated gloves
    if the family of the good is gloves
    and the good has a coating of plastics.

rule group_coated_gloves_rubber with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Impregnated, coated, covered or laminated with plastics or rubber":
the subheading group of a good is coated gloves
    if the family of the good is gloves
    and the good has a coating of rubber
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a coating of plastics.

rule group_gloves with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61, confer "Gloves, mittens and mitts, knitted or crocheted":
the subheading group of a good is gloves
    if the family of the good is gloves
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a coating of plastics
    and it is not the case that
        the good has a coating of rubber.

% Chapter 62 note 8: a scarf, square or nearly so, of which no side exceeds 60
% centimetres, is a handkerchief; a handkerchief with a side over 60 cm is
% classified with the scarves
rule note_62_8_small_scarf with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Scarves and articles of the scarf type, square or approximately square, of which no side exceeds 60 centimeters, are to be classified as handkerchiefs (heading 6213)":
a good is a small square scarf
    if the family of the good is scarf
    and the good is approximately square
    and the longest side of the good measures a number centimetres
    and the number <= 60.

rule note_62_8_large_handkerchief with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Handkerchiefs of which any side exceeds 60 centimeters are to be classified in heading 6214":
a good is a large handkerchief
    if the family of the good is handkerchief
    and the longest side of the good measures a number centimetres
    and the number > 60.

rule group_handkerchief with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62, confer "Handkerchiefs":
the subheading group of a good is handkerchief
    if the family of the good is handkerchief
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a large handkerchief.

rule group_small_scarf with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "are to be classified as handkerchiefs (heading 6213)":
the subheading group of a good is handkerchief
    if the good is a small square scarf.

rule group_scarf with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Shawls, scarves, mufflers, mantillas, veils and the like":
the subheading group of a good is scarf
    if the family of the good is scarf
    and it is not the case that
        the good is a small square scarf.

rule group_large_handkerchief with provenance HTSUS Chapter 62,
        confer "Handkerchiefs of which any side exceeds 60 centimeters are to be classified in heading 6214":
the subheading group of a good is scarf
    if the good is a large handkerchief.
